  #block(breakable: false)[
  === Complete Solutions

  #sol-item(1, "C", dense: true, pad: 15.31pt)[
    Bookkeeping records and classifies; accounting designs the system, reports and interprets the result.
  ]

  #sol-item(2, "C", dense: true, pad: 15.31pt)[
    The firm intends to keep the machine (going concern) and records it at what it cost (historical cost).
  ]
  ]

  #sol-item(3, "A", dense: true, pad: 15.31pt)[
    Under the business entity concept, private spending is drawings, not an expense.
  ]

  #sol-item(4, "C", dense: true, pad: 15.31pt)[
    Liabilities = assets − capital = 920,000 − 540,000 = ₦380,000.
  ]

  #sol-item(5, "C", dense: true, pad: 15.31pt)[
    The debtor rises (debit) and the income is credited.
  ]

  #sol-item(6, "A", dense: true, pad: 15.31pt)[
    The van is an asset and the unpaid supplier is a liability, so both sides of the equation rise by the same amount.
  ]

  #sol-item(7, "B", dense: true, pad: 15.31pt)[
    An item too small to affect a decision may be expensed rather than capitalised.
  ]

  #sol-item(8, "A", dense: true, pad: 15.31pt)[
    700,000 − 120,000 + 80,000 = ₦660,000.
  ]

  #sol-item(9, "A", dense: true, pad: 15.31pt)[
    The buyer debits the seller's account, so the document is a debit note.
  ]

  #sol-item(10, "A", dense: true, pad: 15.31pt)[
    The purchases day book lists credit purchases from invoices received.
  ]

  #sol-item(11, "B", dense: true, pad: 15.31pt)[
    Corrections and other non-routine entries belong in the general journal.
  ]

  #sol-item(12, "C", dense: true, pad: 15.31pt)[
    The debits exceed the credits by ₦45,000, which is entered on the credit side of the suspense account.
  ]

  #sol-item(13, "D", dense: true, pad: 15.31pt)[
    A provision is a credit balance, deducted from debtors in the statement of financial position.
  ]

  #sol-item(14, "D", dense: true, pad: 15.31pt)[
    It is an arithmetic check on the double entry and nothing more.
  ]

  #sol-item(15, "B", dense: true, pad: 15.31pt)[
    It carries the totals posted from the day books and checks the personal ledger.
  ]

  #sol-item(16, "C", dense: true, pad: 15.31pt)[
    260,000 + 980,000 − 870,000 − 25,000 − 10,000 = ₦335,000.
  ]

  #sol-item(17, "A", dense: true, pad: 15.31pt)[
    540,000 + 35,000 − 90,000 = ₦485,000.
  ]

  #sol-item(18, "B", dense: true, pad: 15.31pt)[
    A charge reduces the firm's money at the bank, so the cash book is credited.
  ]

  #sol-item(19, "D", dense: true, pad: 15.31pt)[
    The bank is owed money that will be settled within the year, so it is a current liability.
  ]

  #sol-item(20, "B", dense: true, pad: 15.31pt)[
    The statement is higher than the truth by the cheques not yet presented.
  ]

  #sol-item(21, "A", dense: true, pad: 15.31pt)[
    50,000 + 280,000 + 20,000 − 60,000 = ₦290,000.
  ]

  #sol-item(22, "B", dense: true, pad: 15.31pt)[
    Cost of sales 60,000 + 340,000 − 80,000 = 320,000; gross profit 580,000 − 320,000 = ₦260,000.
  ]

  #sol-item(23, "C", dense: true, pad: 15.31pt)[
    Carriage outwards is the cost of delivering goods to the customer.
  ]

  #sol-item(24, "B", dense: true, pad: 15.31pt)[
    90,000 − 15,000 + 20,000 = ₦95,000.
  ]

  #sol-item(25, "C", dense: true, pad: 15.31pt)[
    15% of ₦1,200,000 = ₦180,000.
  ]

  #sol-item(26, "D", dense: true, pad: 15.31pt)[
    New provision 12,000 less existing 5,000 = ₦7,000.
  ]

  #sol-item(27, "D", dense: true, pad: 15.31pt)[
    Only the part that belongs to next year is carried forward as a prepayment.
  ]

  #sol-item(28, "D", dense: true, pad: 15.31pt)[
    (720,000 − 300,000) ÷ 280,000 = 1.5 : 1.
  ]

  #sol-item(29, "A", dense: true, pad: 15.31pt)[
    Cost of sales rises by the omitted stock, so gross profit falls.
  ]

  #sol-item(30, "B", dense: true, pad: 15.31pt)[
    They reduce the owner's stake; they are not a cost of trading.
  ]

  #sol-item(31, "B", dense: true, pad: 15.31pt)[
    Both sides are equally wrong, so the totals still agree.
  ]

  #sol-item(32, "C", dense: true, pad: 15.31pt)[
    The same wrong figure was entered on both sides, so the columns still agree although the ledger is wrong.
  ]

  #sol-item(33, "D", dense: true, pad: 15.31pt)[
    Income was recorded too high, so profit is too high.
  ]

  #sol-item(34, "A", dense: true, pad: 15.31pt)[
    The missing amount must be added to the credit column, so suspense is credited.
  ]

  #sol-item(35, "C", dense: true, pad: 15.31pt)[
    The statutory default is equal shares.
  ]

  #sol-item(36, "C", dense: true, pad: 15.31pt)[
